hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2737","Narrated to us Al-Hasan ibn az-Za'farani, narrated to us Sa'id ibn Sulayman, narrated to us 'Abdullah ibn al-Mu'ammal, who heard 'Ata' narrate from 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr (RA) that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:

""The Black Stone will come on the Day of Resurrection with a tongue and two lips, and it will testify in favor of whoever touched it with sincere intention. It is the right hand of Allah with which He shakes the hands of His creation.""

**CHAPTER:**"
